  "term": "pseudohypoparathyroidism",
  "definition": "Pseudohypoparathyroidism is a genetic condition caused by an inactivating mutation in the GNAS gene; when the mutation is maternally inherited, it can produce pseudohypoparathyroidism type 1a. In the source packet, all studied patients with this form showed intellectual disability, making it relevant to cognition.",
